      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to notice the volatility in battery tech and lithium; this is a classic case of \"transition risk\" where the market is still figuring out the scale of the shift, creating a temporary but intense price spike that will eventually normalize as supply chains mature. The massive capital sunk into old fossil fuel infrastructure is indeed a gamble, but it is a calculated one because the sheer volume of existing assets creates a multi-decade revenue stream that no amount of climate rhetoric can erase overnight. While the transition is painful and creates short-term chaos for both sectors, the long-term trajectory is undeniable: the world is moving toward renewables, and the volatility you see is simply the friction of that inevitable change.",
