      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if the transition is \"inevitable\" and \"undeniable\" like you say, then what's the argument for staying heavily invested in oil and gas? i'm seeing people say that the tech just isn't there yet to handle base load power on its own, and that forcing the transition too fast will just crash the economy. is that just \"climate denialism\" or is there a legitimate economic case to be made there?",
